        "original_id": "883cd981-2275-55c4-966a-6edf544c03dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dawn French, Jennifer Saunders, Al Pillay, Lana Pellay, Adrian Edmondson, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, Robbie Coltrane, Gary Clail\n- Works: The Supergrass, French and Saunders, The Vicar of Dibley, Eat the Rich, The Comic Strip Presents, Gino, Human Nature, Emotional Hooligan\n- Roles: actress, writer, comedian, backing vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- Dawn Roma French was born on 11 October 1957 and is an English actress, writer, and comedian.\n- Al Pillay was born on 22 August 1959 and is also known by the names Alana Pellay and Lana Pellay.\n- Dawn French is best known for starring in and writing French and Saunders with Jennifer Saunders.\n- Dawn French also played the lead role of Geraldine Granger in The Vicar of Dibley.\n- Al Pillay starred in Eat the Rich.\n- In The Comic Strip Presents, Al Pillay appeared as Alan Pellay playing himself in Gino and as Alana Pellay playing herself in episode 13.\n- Al Pillay appeared as Lana Pellay playing Mary in the feature film The Supergrass.\n- The film The Supergrass starred Richardson, Adrian Edmondson, Jennifer Saunders, Dawn French, Keith Allen, Nigel Planer, Alexei Sayle, Ronald Allen, and Robbie Coltrane.\n- The song Human Nature by Gary Clail On-U Sound System features Lana Pellay on backing vocals.\n- Human Nature can be found on the album Emotional Hooligan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
